WEBVTT

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:02.100
Georgie!

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:04.800
What am I supposed to write here?

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.610
I just gave you the materials.

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.000
Yeah, but they went somewhere.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:09.660
You mean these?

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.770
Thanks, Sumi.

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:14.060
Sumi?

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.290
I brought back the opinion box.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:18.740
Thanks, senpai.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:22.000
<b>Opinion Box</b>

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:20.270
Thanks for your hard work, too.

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.000
What's an opinion box?

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.660
It's a suggestion box for people 
to submit their opinions

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.140
concerning the Hoshi Festival.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.690
Although it doesn't seem to 
be getting much use right now.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:33.380
Ichijoji, the principal wants to see you.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:34.660
Yes, sir.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:35.890
Aigasaki.

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:36.390
Huh?

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.390
I'll let you handle the opinion box.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.280
Me?

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.140
Got it.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.520
Keep up the good work, guys.

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:50.020
All right. I'll get this—

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:53.400
Um...

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:56.630
So many.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:57.820
Yeah.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.410
I'm sure I can do it. Right?

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:02.720
Aigasaki-senpai.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:03.330
Yes?

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:05.870
I'll help you.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:26.160
<b>Magic-Kyun! Renaissance</b>

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:41.010
I Just Can't Ignore You, Senpai!

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:47.890
Let me take one more.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:53.970
Introductions for the committee members, huh?

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:56.110
So even that's necessary.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:58.110
Hoshi Festival Opinion

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:58.110
Who are the members of the 
Hoshi festival committee this year?

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:58.110
Third-Year, Major: Glassblowing

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:58.110
I had no idea.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:00.230
Kanato-kun, you're all set.

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:03.240
You're next, Anjo-senpai.

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:04.990
Okay.

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:06.870
Say "cheese."

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:11.750
How was that?

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:13.250
Don't look.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:15.740
Try to act normal.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:17.760
What? But I was trying so hard.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.770
Your efforts aren't pointed 
in the right direction.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:21.220
Suminomiya-kun, are you ready to go next?

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:22.390
You think so?

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:24.870
Suminomiya-kun?

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:27.770
I'm not used to this sort of thing.

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:29.640
I don't know what to do.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:32.020
Just be yourself.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:33.940
Be myself?

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:35.840
Yeah, act natural.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:37.230
Natural.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:42.870
Natural?

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:44.880
That's more unnatural.

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.280
You...

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.410
We don't have time to mess around.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:51.550
W-We weren't messing around.

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:54.670
Yeah. Why don't you help us, Senpai?

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.170
What?

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.050
Say "cheese."

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:04.800
Too stiff.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.180
He's kind of scary.

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:09.430
Georgie, it's important to smile.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:11.310
I know.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.310
Say "cheese."

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:18.820
<i>What am I, a child?</i>

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:21.700
Suminomiya-senpai.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.570
<b>Smile</b>

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:24.570
<i>I know!</i>

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:28.930
The corners of your mouth are the 
most important part of your smile.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:30.910
Just like this.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:34.920
Don't be shy. Come on.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:38.170
Three, two, one.

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:48.930
Ichijoji-kun, it's a miracle.

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:51.020
Let's get back to work.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:52.740
Okay.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:57.190
Monet, I made you a cupcake for today's snack.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:04:59.430
Is it sweet?

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:01.190
Not really.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:08.170
See? Even Rinsuke says it's okay.

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:10.320
It's good. Why don't you eat some?

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:11.200
Okay.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:28.340
It's... good.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.780
All right!

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:37.350
What?

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:39.250
You finally ate some.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:42.010
There are carrots in that.

00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:44.410
I completely hid the smell.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.860
Not even you noticed it.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:51.050
Who said I don't like carrots?

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.650
You did!

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:54.620
The Hoshi Festival, huh?

00:05:54.890 --> 00:05:56.330
What are they doing this year?

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:58.370
The king is leading the committee?

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:00.910
They're the ones running 
the Art Session, right?

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:02.630
Hoshi Festival News
Announcing This Year's Committee Members!!

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:02.630
I'm so excited.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:05.740
They're excited.

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:08.010
It's got nothing to do with us, though.

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:14.770
Here are the rules for participating 
in the Hoshi Festival.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:16.520
Thanks for getting them for me.

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:18.790
It's okay. I was already working.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:20.800
By the way, I saw your poster.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:22.560
Really? What did you think?

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:25.090
Everyone's talking about it.

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:26.420
I think it went over pretty well.

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:29.810
That's great. It's probably 
because of Kanato-kun.

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:31.840
Oh, that tall guy?

00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:33.300
He plays the cello, right?

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:33.950
Yeah.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:37.080
Does he have time for that?

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:38.130
What?

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:40.070
He has a recital coming up.

00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:42.240
Everyone else is practicing a ton.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:43.720
He must have plenty of time to spare.

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:48.970
Sorry, Kanato-kun.

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:52.860
I had no idea you had a recital.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:56.800
It's fine. I've been practicing hard.

00:06:56.800 --> 00:06:57.980
What? Really?

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:00.100
I'll be totally fine.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:02.980
Anyway, let's try to get a lot done today.

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:05.650
What should we start with?

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:07.360
Oh, well...

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:10.150
We've been asked to hold 
consultation meetings.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:15.620
Hoshi Festival
 Consultations

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:15.620
We're the Hoshi Festival committee!

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:17.620
Is there anything you'd like to ask about?

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.870
There are 66 days until 
this year's Hoshi Festival.

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:22.980
You should start preparing early.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.700
Angelo, what are you guys going to be doing?

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:27.890
You'll find out the day of the festival.

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:30.020
Aw!

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:30.990
Hoshi Festival Consultations

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:33.180
Um... We'd like to open a cafe.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:34.850
How would we go about that?

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:36.640
A cafe?

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:40.100
You should choose good beans.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:40.900
What?

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:42.690
Their freshness is important.

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:44.930
Beans four days after roasting are best.

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:46.880
I recommend Nicaraguan beans.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:50.110
They have a robust and rich flavor and 
make decent paste for brushes, too.

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:51.740
They're perfect for calligraphy.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:53.410
Calligraphy?

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:55.430
Please write down what 
you'll need on this form

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:57.740
and submit it to the committee.

00:07:58.070 --> 00:07:59.530
Next problem.

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:00.120
Okay.

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:01.620
Next is...

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:04.120
The refreshment stands can't 
agree on what to serve.

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:05.670
We should serve pancakes.

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:06.960
No, we should serve takoyaki.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.510
The seaweed will get everywhere.

00:08:08.510 --> 00:08:10.510
Well, pancakes are just sweet.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:15.110
Senpai, how many applications did we receive 
for pancake stands and takoyaki stands?

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:16.480
Let's see.

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:17.980
Two applications for pancake stands,

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:19.700
and two for takoyaki stands.

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:21.210
They'd be doubling up.

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:24.020
How would you feel about crepes?

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.600
Crepes?

00:08:27.140 --> 00:08:30.400
Crepes are sweet like pancakes,

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.610
and they're no substitute for takoyaki.

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:36.680
You can make crepes with savory ingredients.

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:38.620
You can put whatever you want in them.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:40.500
That sounds great!

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:42.620
That might not be a bad idea.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:47.000
<i>They agreed on an idea?</i>

00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:51.510
The parade doesn't have enough participants.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:55.590
Apparently we don't have enough 
people to carry the shrine.

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:57.090
Could you help us out?

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.720
We can't refuse a request from you, Kanato.

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:03.320
Guys, let's lend him a hand.

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:04.100
Yeah!

00:09:04.550 --> 00:09:05.330
Thank you.

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:06.350
We appreciate the help.

00:09:07.010 --> 00:09:09.570
<i>Kanato-kun is so well connected.</i>

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:12.320
Next problem.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:12.860
Let's see.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:15.240
They can't get the stains 
out of their uniforms.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:18.240
You should wash out dirt stains by hand.

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:22.370
The futsal team doesn't have enough members.

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:25.620
The roof is leaking badly.

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:29.000
All better!

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.500
That didn't have anything to 
do with the Hoshi Festival.

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:36.360
Yeah, but I had fun.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:38.140
And everyone was happy about it.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:39.650
Really?

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:42.380
If you don't mind, then I guess I don't either.

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:53.780
I can't believe I took so long 
to notice I forgot something.

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:06.070
The school is kind of creepy at night.

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:35.030
<i>Kanato-kun's practicing so late.</i>

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:47.410
For you.

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:49.140
Magic-Kyun.

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:52.480
Magic-Kyun.

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:54.470
Renaissance.

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:00.800
Thanks for the food.

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:03.540
Cu-Cu-Curry.

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:08.810
Kanato-kun.

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:11.350
Oh, Senpai. What's up?

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:12.370
I know this is sudden,

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:14.850
but thanks for all your help with everything.

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:16.630
I'm sorry I keep asking for your help

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:18.070
when you're already so busy.

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:20.350
Where did that come from?

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:22.320
I've been thinking.

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:26.080
Kanato-kun, I'll try doing the rest on my own.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:29.230
What? But there's only one thing left.

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:30.350
Leave it to me.

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:32.810
I think you're being reckless.

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:34.830
That's not true.

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:36.090
Are you sure?

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:37.090
Yeah.

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:39.970
It's ghost busting.

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:41.970
Huh?

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:44.340
What?!

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:09.400
Sorry, Kanato-kun.

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:11.680
I needed your help until the very end after all.

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:13.230
It's fine.

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:15.710
Since it could be dangerous, I'm 
glad you're not doing it alone.

00:12:16.570 --> 00:12:18.210
Anyway, Senpai...

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:20.460
Wh-What?

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:23.970
Apparently ghosts appear 
if you tell scary stories.

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:25.870
S-So?

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:27.580
So we'll use these!

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:33.230
Now you'll be okay.

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:35.410
Uh, yeah. Thanks.

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:36.980
Senpai, look.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:39.380
I brought a bunch of other things, too.

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:41.030
Holy salt.

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:42.370
Talismans.

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:43.960
A mirror.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:45.970
Sterilizing spray.

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:47.880
Apparently it's super effective.

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:49.030
O-Okay.

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:52.040
Anyway, I'm excited.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:52.670
<i>What?</i>

00:12:52.670 --> 00:12:54.350
It's the real thing.

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:55.230
Don't you want to see it?

00:12:55.230 --> 00:12:56.500
No!

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.100
According to rumors,

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:02.850
a long-haired woman dressed in white

00:13:02.850 --> 00:13:06.760
wanders around the school at night.

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:13.200
Wh-Why would you bring that up now?

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:15.320
Oh, sorry. I couldn't help myself.

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:20.650
Oh, it's just a cat.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:24.660
I thought my heart was going to stop.

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:26.660
You're such a scaredy-cat.

00:13:28.420 --> 00:13:29.220
Senpai.

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:32.140
I'm here for you.

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:46.080
Kanato-kun, don't!

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:48.440
If you touch it, it'll start moving!

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:50.400
It's just a statue.

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:51.720
Oh...

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:59.760
This seems like some place you'd find them.

00:13:59.760 --> 00:14:00.980
F-Find what?

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:10.120
S-Something's on the back of my head.

00:14:08.690 --> 00:14:11.930
Calm down. It's just a spiderweb.

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:19.600
Senpai, I'm sorry.

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:22.500
I should've done this by myself.

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:25.680
No, I'm sorry.

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:28.320
You've been practicing so hard,

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:30.390
I wanted you to take a break.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:33.960
You were that worried about me?

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:37.040
I'm fine. I'm doing it because I want to.

00:14:37.420 --> 00:14:38.390
But...

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:41.570
I'll do everything I can.

00:14:41.570 --> 00:14:43.400
Just let me know what you need.

00:14:44.810 --> 00:14:46.780
You're amazing, Kanato-kun.

00:14:47.010 --> 00:14:48.650
You help everyone solve their problems,

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:50.720
and you're good at getting people to agree.

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:57.000
That's because I've been taking care 
of my siblings since I was little.

00:14:57.610 --> 00:15:00.290
What I learned doing that must be paying off.

00:15:00.990 --> 00:15:02.640
Really?

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:09.620
I've been wondering if there's 
something I can do to thank you.

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:12.550
But the way things are going, 
I doubt there's anything I can do.

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:15.270
Aigasaki-senpai, you're so nice.

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:17.310
That's not true.

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:18.240
Huh?

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:19.220
What?

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:23.860
It's out of batteries.

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:25.570
What? What are we going to do?

00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:31.270
What's wrong?

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:32.900
I hear something.

00:15:32.900 --> 00:15:33.700
What?

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:41.830
Footsteps?

00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:43.310
Senpai.

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:55.300
Senpai, take this.

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:56.100
What?

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:18.740
Begone, evil spirit!

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:22.160
What are you doing, you idiot?

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:23.460
Senpai, stay behind me!

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:24.760
Senpai?

00:16:26.410 --> 00:16:27.590
Hey!

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:30.590
What are you two doing?

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:31.860
S-Sensei?

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:33.140
What are you doing here?

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:36.100
Huh? Patrolling the building, obviously.

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:39.850
Oh, good. You're not a ghost.

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:41.100
What?

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:43.520
We came to get rid of a ghost.

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:44.610
A ghost?

00:16:44.610 --> 00:16:45.480
Yes.

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:48.730
Long-haired and dressed in white,

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:52.240
it wanders around the school every night.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:55.140
They were talking about you.

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:56.320
Oh.

00:16:56.890 --> 00:16:58.550
You kids...

00:16:58.550 --> 00:17:00.180
Sorry.

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:03.120
Sheesh.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:04.820
That was awful.

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:06.880
I'm really sorry.

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.610
I'm sorry.

00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:11.200
That's what you've been up to?

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:12.130
Now, now.

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:14.870
Thanks to them, the committee 
has gained visibility.

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:16.130
Isn't that a good thing?

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:21.010
Hoshi Festival News
Ghost of the East Building Busted!

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:19.360
Apparently the executive 
committee exorcised a ghost.

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:21.010
Seriously?

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:25.840
Yeah. Writing an article about the 
ghost was Aigasaki-senpai's idea.

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:27.430
I didn't do anything.

00:17:27.430 --> 00:17:29.400
You did most of the work, Kanato-kun.

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:32.260
Nobody busted me.

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:33.490
A restligeist?

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:34.400
Who are you talking about?

00:17:34.690 --> 00:17:37.280
In any case, good work this time.

00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:39.570
Thanks. I'm relieved.

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:41.530
Aigasaki, Hibiki.

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:42.790
Yes, sir.

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:45.290
Good job.

00:17:47.740 --> 00:17:48.790
However...

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:50.930
Don't relax yet.

00:17:50.930 --> 00:17:54.550
We still have mountains of work to 
do like making pamphlets and posters.

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:57.680
And we're still missing 
some committee members.

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:01.450
I know. Let's keep working.

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:02.730
What should we do next?

00:18:02.730 --> 00:18:03.850
Kanato, you can rest.

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:04.680
What?

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:07.450
Isn't your recital coming up?

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:09.310
You should focus on your cello.

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:10.510
But—

00:18:10.510 --> 00:18:12.740
Anjo-senpai is right.

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:16.070
It's my turn to return the favor.

00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:18.180
Senpai.

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:21.120
<b>Helping Each Other</b>

00:18:19.460 --> 00:18:21.120
Helping each other.

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:26.120
It's only natural for an Artista 
to prepare for a recital.

00:18:29.230 --> 00:18:31.030
Let us handle the rest.

00:18:33.570 --> 00:18:36.160
Got it. Thank you!

00:18:41.230 --> 00:18:42.640
Sorry.

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:45.410
I feel like I've inconvenienced 
the rest of you.

00:18:45.410 --> 00:18:48.890
Not at all. Let us know if you need anything.

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:51.160
You don't need to do that.

00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:52.590
There's no need to hold back.

00:18:52.590 --> 00:18:55.320
If there's anything I can do, I'll do it.

00:18:55.840 --> 00:18:56.900
Senpai.

00:18:57.220 --> 00:19:00.410
Although I'm not sure I can be of much help.

00:19:01.210 --> 00:19:02.410
In that case,

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:08.150
I'm actually not too confident in the 
song I'm playing for the recital.

00:19:08.150 --> 00:19:10.170
Would you listen to it for me?

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:12.320
Okay.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:41.710
<i>Let's take the first step</i>

00:19:41.710 --> 00:19:45.030
<i>It's all right</i>

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:48.410
<i>I'll never let go</i>

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:53.490
<i>Of your hand</i>

00:19:57.920 --> 00:20:01.380
<i>Broad skies and vast seas</i>

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:04.720
<i>Take a deep breath</i>

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:09.780
<i>And towards new dreams, let's go!</i>

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:14.850
<i>We'll reach as far as the sun</i>

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:17.610
<i>With our special magic</i>

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:23.710
<i>I want you to be the first to see it</i>

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:31.680
<i>If you feel uneasy when you're alone</i>

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:38.040
<i>Then call me! I'll come running</i>

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:41.920
<i>A seven-colored shining rainbow star</i>

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:45.260
<i>Together, we'll fly beyond</i>

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:52.020
<i>Towards views we've never seen before!</i>

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:55.440
<i>Don't worry, flower star</i>

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:58.820
<i>I'll always be by your side</i>

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:07.850
<i>I promise to protect you</i>

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:17.580
Senpai.

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:18.250
Yes?

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:23.020
If we're together, we'll put on
 the best Hoshi Festival ever.

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:24.650
So...

00:21:25.810 --> 00:21:27.390
Let's work hard together.

00:21:27.920 --> 00:21:28.800
Yeah.

00:23:21.500 --> 00:23:22.880
Thank you.

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:28.800
How can you work so hard for someone else?

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:30.010
It's so weird.

00:23:30.420 --> 00:23:33.220
It's not like I really care or anything.

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:36.000
Next time on Magic-Kyun! Renaissance:

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Blown by a Mischievous Wind</b>

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:37.840
"Blown by a Mischievous Wind."

00:23:37.840 --> 00:23:39.020
Magic-Kyun for you.
